From 9c782d0e33f0da236ca4d16e82db93d5db54a6ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:41:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: quote depth for open-quote and close-quote
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every quote used the outermost pair, so nested <q> showed “outer “inner”” instead of
“outer ‘inner’”, 「外側「内側」」 instead of 「外側『内側』」 in Japanese, and custom `quotes` lists
never reached their second pair. The depth at a pseudo-element is now computed by walking the
document in tree order through the rendered ::before/::after content up to it, as the counter
implementation does; levels past the end of the list reuse its last pair, and a close-quote at
depth zero renders nothing, per css-content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
